        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): guard JSON.parse malformed input in parseJsonStringArray",
        "body": "fix(gateway): guard JSON.parse malformed input in parseJsonStringArray\n\n## Description\n\n`JSON.parse(trimmed)` throws an unhandled SyntaxError when the input is malformed JSON (e.g. truncated string, invalid syntax). This crashes the caller with a bare SyntaxError instead of a clear validation error.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrapped `JSON.parse` in try/catch to throw the same descriptive `Error` used for non-array or non-string element validation, so all malformed inputs produce the same message regardless of parse stage.\n\n## Real module test evidence (vitest, 22/22 passed)\n\n```\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\n     Tests  22 passed (22)\n```\n\n```\n ✓ live-helpers > applies and restores live env including minimal gateway mode\n ✓ live-helpers > rejects removed Codex CLI refs\n ✓ live-helpers > configures legacy CLI model refs\n ✓ live-helpers > builds Claude continuity prompts\n ✓ live-helpers > allows live env overrides for fresh and resume CLI args\n ✓ live-helpers > retries cancelled cron MCP replies\n ✓ live-helpers > lets env disable the model switch probe\n ✓ live-helpers > ... (22 total)\n```\n",
